  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia - Strategic Sector Cooperation Agriculture and Food Safety - Phase I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Sector Cooperation in Agriculture and Food Safety Between Denmark and Indonesia, Phase I

Phase I of the cooperation will focus on: 
1) the formulation of a policy framework in the development of organic milk in Indonesia; 2) the formulation of Indonesia&apos;s organic national standards that are comprehensive, in line with international standard and can be implemented especially for small-medium dairy farmers;  3) the implementation of standards and policies compiled in the form of development pilot projects organic milk in a potential dairy farmers cooperative; and 4) capacity building for government officials to implement good practices for organic dairy milk to increase farmer&#x2019;s motivation and welfare.

Denmark is a frontrunner in innovative sustainable and effective food production, with extensive knowledge and technical solutions that Indonesia could benefit from.</narrative>
  </description>
